.TH NAVI-DEFAULTS 1 2026-11-27 Navi "Navi Manual"
.nh
.SH NAME
navi-defaults \- choose which programs open your files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B navi-defaults
.br
.B navi-defaults list
.RI [ category ]
.br
.B navi-defaults set
.I category program
.br
.B navi-defaults reset
.I category
.SH DESCRIPTION
Run
.B navi-defaults
by itself to pick a category, then a program, from a menu.
The menu lists the installed programs that can open that kind of file.
.PP
Your choices are saved in
.IR ~/.config/mimeapps.list ,
the standard place for them, so they also apply in other desktops.
Navi's own defaults are in
.I /etc/xdg/navi-mimeapps.list
and only apply in Navi, when you haven't chosen something else.
.SH CATEGORIES
Web browser, Videos, Music, Images, PDFs and books, Text files.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B navi-defaults set Videos vlc
Open videos with VLC.
.TP
.B navi-defaults reset Videos
Go back to Navi's default for videos.
